"""Interpret source screens without changing scientific eligibility."""
from pathlib import Path
import pandas as pd
O=Path('outputs/dataset_inventory_20261101')
ROWS=[
('pisco_fish','D01','Counts, lengths, water-column effort and revisits','29,792 sheephead rows: eight positive-count records lack positive lengths; no exact repeated full rows. In standard UCSB/VRG all-taxon survey opportunities, 85 of 1,985 site-years have unequal numbers of non-canopy levels across units; 181 unit-years have more than one survey date. These are full-delivery flags, not counts of affected primary comparisons.','Rules approved; review rerun verified; paper promotion pending','Targeted audit reproduces34 histories at17 retained PISCO comparisons. Repeat averaging changes fitted recovery only at Abalone Cove and Point Vicente. Retain CNMD as a recognized protocol; literal MID-only filtering removes INNER-zone coverage. Follow-up supports retaining144 complete CRANE2004 units;67 single-pass units in paired windows include3 explicitly omitted bottom passes and64 unexplained absences. Recommend excluding incomplete units only from the combined response while preserving measured passes. Approved combined rerun retains175 histories and3225 annual rows; six PISCO sheephead recovery comparisons change without sign reversals; other taxa unchanged. See ../pisco_fish_rules_20261101/README.md.','Source code 04_pisco_processing.R:813-873 omits dates in annual sums and zero-fills numeric NAs; current paper impact not established by this screen.'),
('pisco_swath','D02','Species absence versus missing measurements; measured quantity','129,064 focal rows include 18 missing counts; 17 occur in HSU and one in UCSB red urchins. UCSB/VRG adult kelp include three positive-count rows without positive stipe sizes. Lobster and urchin size meanings differ: a blank swath size is not automatically unusable density.','Open: response-specific missingness and effort','Use actual completed survey events to establish zeros; retain missing count/stipe flags. Aggregate repeated dates as visits before annual means. Link separate size surveys only where biomass needs them.','Prior source reconciliation identifies the retained Vicente kelp, Scorpion red-urchin and South Point sheephead problems; no new values recovered.'),
('mbon_fish','D03','Program/method separation and area','Focal integrated fish contain no exact repeated full rows and all recorded areas are positive. KFM visualfish has 4,326 sheephead records, areas 100 or 200 m2 and no missing counts; KFM roving counts have 404 missing counts among 2,967 records and area 2,000 m2. These methods must remain distinct.','Partly addressed; inspect visit weighting in final roster','Keep visualfish as its own density history. Verify changes in area and repeated dates at the actual site-year level; do not treat a roving count or separate size survey as a missing visual transect.','Current seasonal audit selects visualfish. Source 05_kfm_processing.R:888-914 retains methods separately but omits date when averaging.'),
('mbon_benthic','D04','Quadrats, band transects, plant codes and changing area','All focal areas are positive. KFM urchin quadrats use 1/2 m2; lobster bands use 40/60 m2. Kelp uses distinct juvenile/adult codes and 1/2/10 m2 protocols. Six missing counts occur in the full focal integrated delivery. No exact repeated full rows.','Area normalization addressed; final footprint still open','Keep program, method, code, date and physical unit through aggregation. Match kelp plant counts to stipes per sampled plant; do not sum alternative protocols as independent abundance. Preserve the juvenile exclusion.','Source code uses recorded area; previous Anacapa audit verified plant-count times sampled stipes arithmetic despite inaccurate source comments.'),
('lter_fish','D05','Count multiplicity, missing sentinels and survey area','All 1,499 sheephead rows have area 80 m2. Ten count rows are negative sentinels; no positive-count rows lack a positive length. No exact repeats or multiple dates within the screened physical-unit/year keys.','Checked in delivery; retain safeguards','Remove sentinels as missing, multiply individual mass by COUNT, and assert area and valid lengths in the final build. The code zero-fill branch is a potential hazard but has no positive-count missing-length case in this delivery.','06_lter_processing.R:797-815 multiplies COUNT by mass; do not label this a currently demonstrated biomass error.'),
('lter_kelp','D06','Plant-level repetition, quadrat identity and area','29,526 rows have positive areas of 20 or 40 m2. Five negative frond sentinels and 130 rows with an incomplete screened physical key. 13,157 rows repeat all delivered fields; without plant IDs, equal plants cannot be distinguished from accidental repeats. Holdfast diameter is not required for the selected stipe conversion.','Open: incomplete physical keys; repetitions are not deletion candidates','Trace incomplete keys and sentinels to the final roster; retain equal-valued plant rows. Sum fronds within measured quadrat/side before area normalization and average within the intended hierarchy.','Use YEAR/SITE/TRANSECT/QUAD/SIDE/AREA; the full-delivery key flags are not automatic exclusions.'),
('lter_lobster','D07','Direct lengths, antenna-only observations and denominator','All 8,341 rows have area 300 m2, with no negative/missing counts or full-row repeats. Six positive-count records lack lengths in the entire delivery: five retained records already receive same-site/date mean mass; one Carpinteria record is outside the two retained primary histories.','Known retained missing lengths addressed','Keep COUNT and antenna-only flag separate; do not add NUM_AO again to COUNT. Preserve imputation flags/donor counts and revisit support if the roster expands.','docs/LOBSTER_MISSING_LENGTHS_2026-10-30.md; code/R/56_lobster_missing_lengths.R'),
('invertebrate_sizes','D08','Frequency weights, sample identity and count-size matching','The complete 335,498-row mixed-code file has 18 negative frequencies, 265,095 incomplete dates and 291,871 rows missing at least one site/zone/transect key. 32,772 full-row repetitions are not necessarily duplicate animals. These totals include nonfocal codes.','Open: final-roster size linkage','Use positive valid frequencies with the appropriate taxon/unit definitions. Label annual pools separately from exact-visit matches; retain shared-pool IDs and propagate shared uncertainty. Do not infer 291,871 lost samples: these surveys need not use the count-transect design.','Existing canonical pool audit covers 15 histories, not all expanded candidates. Audit eligibility and donor coverage before final biomass refits.'),
('kfm_kelp_sizes','D09','Plants, stipes and numeric station crosswalk','65,215 plant-size rows have positive stipe counts and complete dates. 18,413 full-row repetitions can represent equal plants; 26,658 diameters are missing/nonpositive but diameter is not needed for the current stipe-based conversion.','Count-size matching still required for final roster','Retain plant rows and link SiteNumber to count-site IDs explicitly. Compare source year/season and adult plant protocol before drawing stipes per plant; document repeated use of donor pools.','Do not divide these plant measurements by quadrat area as if they were independent abundance surveys.'),
('landsat_annual','D10','Missing canopy, empty masks and annual summaries','The 60-row harmonized delivery contains 96 missing annual cells and 350 explicit zeros. The separately indexed full supplier delivery has 72 polygon slots: 58 nonempty arrays and 14 empty slots. No negative values in the screened annual table.','Mask repair addressed; reference composition and temporal support remain','Keep valid zero canopy distinct from invalid imagery/empty masks. Track which reference polygons contribute each year, pixel/area weighting, and whether annual maxima represent different quarters; evaluate current rebuilt arrays rather than interpreting old delivery flags as new model defects.','Previous pixel/mask verification is retained; quarterly reconstruction was not repeated in this measurement audit.')]
EXTRA=[
('Q01','Visits and survey effort','PISCO fish/swath; integrated surveys','Before response rebuild','Some source aggregation keys omit full dates; repeat visits and changing fish levels exist in the raw delivery.','For the final roster, prove one effort-normalized value per physical visit before annual aggregation; retain surveyed absences separately from missing responses.','measurement_design_scan.csv; pisco_fish_level_coverage.csv; pisco_fish_revisited_units.csv'),
('Q02','Weighting and changing station support','All diver programs','Before response rebuild','Equal transect, zone, station or sampled-area weights answer different questions; additional visits must not silently give a site more weight.','Specify each averaging step and use a fixed prediction population. Compare actual sampled support through time, without selecting rules by effect direction.','Source processing code 04/05/06; candidate_pair_coverage.csv'),
('Q03','Nonlinear biomass conversion','All size-derived biomass','Before final biomass fit','Mass from an average length differs from the average mass of measured individuals; frequency counts and shared donor pools matter.','Verify per-animal/bin mass and frequency weighting, units and donor linkage for each retained taxon; extend the existing uncertainty ledger to the final roster.','measurement_protocols.csv; supporting_source_inventory.csv'),
('Q04','Detection and protocol changes','Fish and lobster counts','Interpretation; sensitivity only if justified','Recorded counts can change with visibility, observer or survey method. Availability of a field does not establish a validated detection correction.','Summarize visibility/observer completeness in the final roster if using them; disclose limits. Do not regress out post-protection habitat changes without deciding the biological estimand.','PISCO raw files contain observer/visibility fields; no detection model was fitted here.'),
('Q05','Zeros and ratio offsets','All log-ratio responses','Before final model freeze','An offset can dominate sparse lobster or depleted kelp ratios and need not cancel when survey support or units change.','Pin one documented offset rule per biological response and units; retain zero frequencies and an offset sensitivity. Do not tune the offset to restore significance.','Existing ratio corrections; measurement_design_scan.csv'),
('Q06','Reference composition and satellite season','Landsat','Before final satellite freeze','An annual maximum can come from different quarters inside/outside, and the number of usable reference polygons can change.','Report current rebuilt-array annual contributors and valid-quarter coverage; keep mask area and total-canopy versus density interpretation explicit.','satellite_full_delivery.csv; prior Landsat verification; quarterly support not rescanned here.')]
def apply(ds,sites):
 a=pd.DataFrame(ROWS,columns=['dataset_id','audit_id','checks','verified_findings','status','next_action','evidence_and_limits']);a.to_csv(O/'dataset_audit.csv',index=False)
 q=pd.DataFrame(EXTRA,columns=['check_id','issue','scope','timing','reason','required_check','evidence']);q.to_csv(O/'additional_analysis_checks.csv',index=False)
 for c in ['audit_id','measurement_audit_status','measurement_audit_next_action']:ds=ds.drop(columns=c,errors='ignore')
 ds=ds.merge(a[['dataset_id','audit_id','status','next_action']].rename(columns={'status':'measurement_audit_status','next_action':'measurement_audit_next_action'}),on='dataset_id',validate='one_to_one')
 ds.to_csv(O/'dataset_inventory.csv',index=False)
 sites=sites.drop(columns='measurement_audit_id',errors='ignore');sites['measurement_audit_id']=sites.dataset_id.map(a.set_index('dataset_id').audit_id)
 # Attach source-screen flags to observed PISCO fish records only. Flags do not change inclusion.
 levels=pd.read_csv(O/'pisco_fish_level_coverage.csv');revisit=pd.read_csv(O/'pisco_fish_revisited_units.csv')
 flags=levels.groupby('site').agg(raw_site_years_unequal_fish_levels=('unequal_level_coverage','sum')).join(revisit.groupby('site').size().rename('raw_fish_revisited_unit_years')).fillna(0)
 for c in flags:
  sites[c]=sites.site_id.map(flags[c]).where(sites.dataset_id.eq('pisco_fish') & sites.inventory_record_type.eq('Observed source/response record'))
 sites.to_csv(O/'site_response_coverage.csv',index=False)
 text='# Dataset measurement and design audit\n\nNovember 1, 2026. All ten inventoried datasets were screened. Source records, exclusions, results and paper remain unchanged. Source totals include sites, methods and taxa outside the primary analysis; a flag is not a demonstrated effect on the paper. No rows were deleted.\n\n'
 for r in a.itertuples():
  text+=f'## {r.audit_id}: {r.dataset_id}\n\n{r.verified_findings}\n\n**Status:** {r.status}.\n\n**Next:** {r.next_action}\n\nEvidence/limits: {r.evidence_and_limits}\n\n'
 text+='## Before freezing\n\nResolve visit/effort aggregation and response-specific missingness on the chosen roster; extend count-size linkage; specify weighting, offsets, dependence and uncertainty. Retain existing researcher exclusions. Repeated equal-valued plants, out-of-scope missing records and unavailable ancillary diameters are not reasons to drop comparisons. Source code was inspected, but current numerical consequences were not estimated. The six additional checks are in additional_analysis_checks.csv.\n\nReproduce: run audit_dataset_measurement_design.py, then report_dataset_inventory.py and verify_dataset_inventory.py. Repeated-unit dates are metadata only, not individual observations. Exact row equality means repeated delivered fields, not proof of accidental duplication. Calendar-year checks compare recorded year to parsed dates; provider campaign differences remain in the separate campaign ledger.\n'
 (O/'DATASET_AUDIT.md').write_text(text)
 return ds,sites
